  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 192, 'Keep watch for a bird taking a dust bath in a dry patch of soil along a path or at the edge of a garden.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 193, 'Discover what a fledgling is, and why a young bird on the ground usually has parents close by.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 194, 'Rake fallen leaves under a shrub instead of bagging them, so sparrows and robins can scratch for food.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 195, 'Map the places you see birds near your home on a small drawing, marking a favorite perch.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 196, 'Spot a fallen feather on your balcony or path and look closely at it right where it lies.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 197, 'Visit a quiet cemetery or churchyard, keep to the paths, and listen to the birds among the trees.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 198, 'Browse pictures of the eggs of one local bird in a library book, and leave real nests alone.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 199, 'Store bird seed in a sealed container so it stays dry and does not draw mice.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 200, 'Tell a family story at dinner about a bird you once saw that stayed with you.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 201, 'Check whether a group of birds on a roof are all facing the same way, and guess why.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 202, 'Pause beside a patch of weeds along a path and see if finches are picking at the seeds.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 203, 'Read up on how long a common bird near you usually lives, and think about the seasons it has already seen.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 204, 'Hang a feeder only where you can reach it from the ground, never with a ladder or a chair.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 205, 'Explore a folk tale or myth from another culture that features a bird.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 206, 'Listen for an alarm call, a sharp repeated note, and look around for what unsettled the birds.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 207, 'Pause by a thick shrub as you walk and listen for the chatter of birds inside, then try to spot one.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 208, 'Observe how a bird takes off: does it jump straight up, run a few steps or drop from a perch?'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 209, 'Choose plain seed without fillers if you feed birds, and skip salty or sugary scraps.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 210, 'Photograph or draw the view you watch birds from, and notice how much it has come to mean to you.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 211, 'Hear how the gulls or crows near your home call back and forth to each other.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 212, 'Find a birdhouse or nest box in a park and watch it from the path for a minute, without going any closer.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 213, 'Pick up the name of one bird in another language you know or are curious about.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 214, 'Spare the spider webs on a porch or fence where you can, since some birds use the silk in their nests.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 215, 'Arrange a few bird pictures from old calendars or cards on a board you see each day.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 216, 'Breathe slowly for three breaths while a bird sits still, and let your body settle the way it does.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 217, 'At the beach, watch small shorebirds run back and forth with the waves, keeping your distance.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 218, 'Look closely at the eye color of a bird you can see clearly, with binoculars if you have them.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 219, 'Find a spot for your water dish with a clear view around it, so birds can watch for cats as they drink.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 220, 'Move your arms like a bird you have watched, gliding, flapping or hopping, when no one is looking.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 221, 'Start a simple list of the kinds of birds you see from home, and add to it whenever a new one appears.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 222, 'Stroll beside a river or stream and see which birds wade in the shallows and which keep to the banks.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 223, 'Watch how one bird moves on a branch, creeping, hopping or hanging upside down, as a clue to its kind.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 224, 'Before you trim a hedge in spring, look gently from a distance for a nest, and wait if you find one.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 225, 'Lend a bird book you enjoyed to a friend, with a note about your favorite page.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 226, 'Keep an eye out for birds following a lawn mower or freshly dug soil in search of insects.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 227, 'Wonder where the birds go on a very hot afternoon, then check the shade and any nearby water.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 228, 'Find out what the birds in your area eat in winter when insects are hard to come by.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 229, 'Choose not to release balloons at a celebration, and suggest bubbles or flags instead.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 230, 'Which bird feels most like you today, and why? Write a sentence about it.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 231, 'Trace a bird''s shadow as it crosses your yard or wall on a sunny afternoon.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 232, 'On a cold, bright morning, notice how the birds you pass seem to make the most of every patch of sun.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 233, 'Name two birds you often hear but rarely see near your work or school, asking someone or using a book.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 234, 'Keep well back from geese or gulls with young, giving them room to move away calmly.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 235, 'Let a child you are with lead a short bird walk on a path, staying right beside them.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 236, 'Spend two quiet minutes at your highest window, watching birds at rooftop height.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 237, 'Visit a community garden and see which birds move among the plants and fences.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 238, 'Discover a little about how birds see color, then look at a bright flower and imagine it through their eyes.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 239, 'Watch where you step on a beach in summer, since some birds nest right on the sand.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 240, 'Watch a nature film about birds with someone at home and talk about one moment you both liked.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 241, 'After a heavy snowfall, look out and see where the birds near home find shelter and food.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 242, 'Observe how the birds near a playground keep their distance from running children.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 243, 'Learn three parts of a bird, the crown, the nape and the rump, then look for them on a pigeon.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 244, 'Point any outdoor lights you need down toward the ground instead of up into the sky.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 245, 'Mail a postcard with a small bird sketch to someone who lives far away.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 246, 'Watch for swallows or swifts swooping over the rooftops on a warm summer evening.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 247, 'Pause by an alley or loading area and notice the birds that make a living in those in between spaces.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 248, 'Look up a bird question you have always wondered about, like how a bird keeps its feathers dry in the rain.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 249, 'Let a watering can drip slowly into your bird dish on a hot day, since moving water can catch a bird''s eye.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 250, 'During a hard moment, look for a bird, then write how it shifted your attention, even a little.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 251, 'In fall, look for birds lining up in big groups on the wires before they move on.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 252, 'While you wait at a crosswalk, glance up for a bird, then turn your full attention back to the traffic.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 253, 'Describe where a bird sits in a tree, at the top, in the middle, on the outer twigs or on the trunk.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 254, 'Grow a pot of dill or parsley on a balcony and let it flower for the insects birds eat.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 255, 'Record a short voice note describing a bird you just watched, and listen back to it later.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 256, 'Stand outside your door on a still spring or fall night and listen for the faint calls of migrating birds passing overhead.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 257, 'Sit in your parked car with the window down for two minutes and listen for birds before you head inside.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 258, 'Size up a bird by comparing it to ones you know: sparrow sized, robin sized or crow sized.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 259, 'Space out your feeders or water dishes so birds are not crowded together, which helps keep them healthy.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 260, 'Compare notes with a neighbor on which birds visit your street.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 261, 'Observe how a robin tilts its head on the lawn before it pulls up a worm.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 262, 'Try a nature trail or park you have never visited, staying on the path, and see which birds live there.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 263, 'Hunt down which birds near you sing in winter too, and listen for one on a cold morning.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 264, 'Set your bird bath low and steady, on the ground or a sturdy stand, so it cannot tip.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 265, 'Browse a library book of bird paintings and pick the one you would hang on your wall.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 266, 'Name to yourself the tree or bush near your home that birds visit most, and wonder what draws them there.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 267, 'Take a photo of a bird from where you stand, without stepping closer, and then just look at it.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 268, 'Add the word crepuscular to your vocabulary, for creatures most active at dusk and dawn, and notice which birds fit.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 269, 'Allow a tree stump or dead branch to stand in your own yard if it is safe, since some birds feed and nest in old wood.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 270, 'List bird words you like the sound of, such as flutter, warble and swoop.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 271, 'Observe how the birds near your home react when a cat or dog wanders by.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 272, 'Spot a bird making a life at a train station or airport among all the travelers.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 273, 'Spot the pigeons on a ledge that puff up their chests and coo at the others.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 274, 'Plant a native shrub with berries in fall, a good time for roots to settle in.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 275, 'Tell a younger family member about a bird you loved watching when you were their age.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 276, 'Hold still for a moment when a bird near your home seems to be watching you back, and share the look.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 277, 'Scout a path or road edge for a bird picking at the gravel, staying well away from traffic.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 278, 'Practice finding a bird you hear by turning your head slowly until the sound is strongest.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 279, 'Put up a nest box in spring only where you can reach it from the ground, and never open it once it is in use.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 280, 'Imagine your street from a bird''s point of view, and write a few lines as if you were flying above it.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 281, 'Wait for a bird to drink and see how it tips its head back to swallow.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 282, 'Stand on the walkway of a bridge over a river and watch the birds below.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 283, 'Research which birds near you nest in holes, and look from the path for round openings in old trees.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 284, 'Join a local park cleanup for an hour, picking up litter along the paths.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 285, 'Volunteer to read a bird book at a library story time or to a child''s class.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 286, 'Ask yourself whether the birds near home tend to come alone, in pairs or in a crowd, then watch to find out.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 287, 'Guess where a diving bird at a waterfront will pop back up, and see if you are right.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 288, 'If gulls live near you, learn how a young gull''s color differs from an adult''s and look for both.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 289, 'Tell a neighbor or coworker about one easy way to stop birds from hitting windows.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 290, 'Set up a small bird corner on a shelf at home with a book, a drawing or a postcard of a bird you love.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 291, 'Pause at the window when you first wake and look for one bird before you check your phone.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 292, 'On the way to work or school, notice whether birds sound different on a bright morning than on a gray one.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 293, 'Glance at the legs and feet of a pigeon or gull and notice what color they are.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 294, 'Close the lid on outdoor trash cans so gulls and crows are not drawn to scraps.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 295, 'At a picnic or outdoor gathering, point out a bird to the group and see who looks up.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 296, 'Before bed, glance out at the dark and think about where the birds near your home might be sleeping.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 297, 'In fall, watch for mixed flocks of small birds moving through the trees in a park.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 298, 'Before bed, read one page of a field guide and pick a bird you hope to spot.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 299, 'Leave a small muddy patch in spring, since robins and swallows use mud to build their nests.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 300, 'Look through old photos for any bird that sneaked into the picture, and share it with whoever was there.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 301, 'Listen for the different sounds of wings: the clatter of a pigeon taking off, the soft whir of a sparrow.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 302, 'Hear how quiet a park is in winter, and pick out a single bird call.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 303, 'Keep a short list of birds you would love to see someday, and read a little about each one.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 304, 'Let some short twigs and dry grass clippings lie in a corner of the yard for spring nest builders.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 305, 'Make a small bird mobile from paper shapes and hang it by a window.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 306, 'Enjoy, from a distance, a young bird near home in summer, fluffy and a little clumsy, trailing after a parent.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 307, 'Stop and listen when you hear a bird you cannot name, and enjoy not knowing.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 308, 'Explore which birds are most often seen in cities and which prefer open country, and think about where you live.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 309, 'Clean out a nest box only once the chicks have left for the season, with gloves on, then wash your hands well.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 310, 'Take a slow fall walk with someone and listen for birds in silence for a few minutes.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 311, 'Spot a bird using your home itself, a gutter, vent, ledge or eave, as a perch or a place to shelter.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 312, 'Notice the birds that linger around a farmers market or outdoor stall.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 313, 'Learn the difference between a pigeon and a dove, and decide which one you see more often.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 314, 'Tip out or cover open buckets, bottles or pipes you can reach, so birds cannot fall in and get stuck.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 315, 'Look back on how the birds you see have changed with the seasons, in a short journal entry.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 316, 'Describe a bird you saw from home to someone who knows birds, and ask what it might be called.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 317, 'Search a park path for signs a bird has eaten there, a pecked apple, a torn pine cone or an empty shell.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 318, 'As fall ends, notice which trees still hold berries and which birds come to visit them.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 319, 'If a bird hits your window, keep pets away, give it quiet, and call a wildlife rescue if it does not fly off.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 320, 'At bedtime, ask a child you look after which bird they would like to be, and why.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 321, 'Wipe the window you watch birds from so the view is a little clearer.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 322, 'Walk outside after a storm passes and notice the birds coming back out to sing.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 323, 'Listen for the difference between a crow''s loud caw and the softer sounds it makes to its family.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 324, 'Brush a small patch of ground clear after snow, near shrubs, so ground feeding birds can reach the soil.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 325, 'Think back on the person who first pointed out a bird to you, and send them a kind word.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 326, 'Enjoy the way low winter sunlight brings out the colors in a bird''s feathers.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 327, 'Glance up at a church steeple, water tower or tall building as you pass and look for birds circling its top.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 328, 'Guess a bird from its silhouette alone as it flies against a bright sky.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 329, 'Bring your feeder in for a while if birds at it look sick, clean it well, wash your hands, and wait before putting it back.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 330, 'Picture the same bird in two seasons and draw it twice, sleek in summer and fluffed up for winter.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 331, 'On a windy day, see how the birds near your home ride the gusts or tuck in out of the wind.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 332, 'Choose a regular bird along your daily route and look for it each time you pass.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 333, 'Sit by an open window one evening and hear when the birds near your home go quiet.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 334, 'Write a short, polite note to your town or building about keeping a green space or old tree that birds use.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 335, 'Spell out a sound a bird made today, like tsip or caw caw, and say it aloud.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 336, 'Tune in to the birds near your home on a gray, still day, and listen to how far their calls seem to carry.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 337, 'Scan the sky above a park in late afternoon and see which birds fly high and which stay low.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 338, 'Search the library shelves for how birds keep their feet from freezing on icy winter branches.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 339, 'Volunteer a little time with a nature center that looks after bird habitat near you.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 340, 'Spend part of a break outside with a coworker, quietly watching whatever birds are around.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 341, 'Listen for a bird near home that repeats one phrase again and again, and notice how long it pauses between.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 342, 'Stop walking before you look up at a bird, so you can keep your footing on wet or icy paths.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 343, 'Compare the steady, rowing flight of a crow with the long, easy glides of a gull.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 344, 'Hold off on flying a kite or drone near flocks of birds resting on a beach or field.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 345, 'Invite a neighbor to enjoy the birds at your shared bird bath or a nearby tree with you.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 346, 'Rest your gaze on a pigeon or crow on a nearby roof and keep watching until it does something new.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 347, 'See whether a group of ducks or geese on a pond keeps one or two watching while the others rest or feed.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 348, 'Seek out the name of one bird that lives mostly in your part of the country, and look at its picture.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 349, 'Use a different door for a while if birds nest by your entrance, so they can raise their chicks in peace.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 350, 'Hang your favorite bird sketch on the fridge or a wall where you will see it each morning.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 351, 'Greet the first birds returning in early spring, and notice which kind reaches your home first.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 352, 'Rest on a bench at the end of a walk and recall each bird you saw.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 353, 'Choose a bird you have come to know well and read a little more about its habits.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 354, 'Make a short list of the bird friendly habits you have started, and pick one to keep up all winter.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 355, 'Gather your thoughts in a short note about what watching birds has given you this year.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 356, 'Look at the birds near your home through a different window than usual, and notice what you see from there.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 357, 'Return to a pond or shoreline path in a new season and notice which birds have come or gone.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 358, 'Turn the pages of a field guide and smile at the birds you have now seen with your own eyes.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 359, 'Carry a reusable cup or bottle when you can, so fewer lids and straws end up where birds feed.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 360, 'Listen to a piece of music inspired by birdsong and notice which parts sound like birds.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 361, 'Thank the birds out your window, quietly, for the few calm minutes they gave you.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 362, 'Carry one bird you saw today in your mind as you head back home.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 363, 'Ask a friend or coworker what bird they see most often, then look up something about it together.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 364, 'Stand quietly where you have helped birds, by a dish, a plant or a clean window, and enjoy whoever comes by.'),
  ('watching-the-birds-around-you', 365, 'Write a short welcome note for someone just starting to notice birds, with the one tip you would give them.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 1, 'Pick one evening this month and write "quiet night" on your calendar in pencil.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 2, 'Take one slow breath before you open your next message today, and let your shoulders soften as you breathe out.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 3, 'Dim the lights in your living room an hour before bed tonight, and notice how the evening slows.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 4, 'Tell someone close to you, in a kind and simple way, that you would love a quiet hour tonight.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 5, 'Notice one small, easy moment with someone today, like a friendly hello, and let yourself enjoy remembering it.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 6, 'Leave a free hour after the next plan on your calendar, so you can wind down at your own pace.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 7, 'Step outside for a minute of fresh air during your next gathering, then head back in when you are ready.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 8, 'After your next gathering, take a warm shower and let the noise of the day rinse away with the water.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 9, 'Introduce two guests who would enjoy each other at a party, then give yourself a breather while they talk.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 10, 'Write down two kinds of time with people that leave you full of energy, and two that tire you out.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 11, 'Settle on a rough time to head home before you arrive at the next party.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 12, 'Sip a glass of water slowly at a party, and use the moment to look around the room.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 13, 'Take a slow walk alone around your block after a long workday, at whatever pace feels easy.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 14, 'Practice one gentle sentence for leaving early, such as "I''ve had a lovely time, and I''m heading home to rest."'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 15, 'Pay attention after your next gathering to how your body feels: your shoulders, your jaw, your eyes.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 16, 'Pack a small bag for your next outing with water, a sweater and a small snack for the trip home.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 17, 'Offer to wash dishes at the next family dinner, and enjoy the quieter few minutes at the sink.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 18, 'Put your phone on quiet for one hour this evening and leave it in another room.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 19, 'Thank a host with a warm message the next morning instead of staying late to say it all in person.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 20, 'Say to yourself tonight, "Needing quiet is part of how I take care of myself, and that''s okay."'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 21, 'Look over your coming plans and circle any days where events sit back to back.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 22, 'Find one person at the party you enjoy and settle into a longer talk with just them.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 23, 'Choose one album you love and listen to it start to finish from a comfortable chair.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 24, 'Ask your roommate what kind of quiet time they like, and share what helps you too.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 25, 'Recall a time you said no to a plan and the friendship stayed just as warm.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 26, 'Move one plan that sits right beside another, so there is a rest gap between them.'),
  ('recharging-after-busy-social-times', 27, 'Leave the gathering at the time you planned, with a warm goodbye to your host.'),
